and you come to a door pretty quickly, and you can just shoot through the door.

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:21.200
I just didn't try that.

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:23.360
I didn't think of that. I was like, oh, maybe I'll go back.

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:25.240
Maybe I missed something. And I went back and went to the left.

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:28.400
Jumped over. Classic Joe move.

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:29.880
Maybe I missed something.

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:31.180
Like, I shouldn't be progressing.

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:32.580
I shouldn't see a door.

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:34.880
I jumped over the thing and got the morph ball,

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:36.840
but I didn't know that I got the morph ball.

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:38.060
So I was like, what was that?

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:39.120
Was that health, or was that?

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:40.440
I was like, I didn't know what that was.

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:42.340
Then I went over, and I was like, oh, a spot.

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:43.640
Let me duck. And I'm like, oh, cool.

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:45.500
You can morph into a ball in this game.

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:49.240
I didn't know that what I had just collected had given me that ability.

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:51.100
So I didn't really know that you were collecting things

00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:54.340
until I got the rockets, which was later on.

00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:55.420
And then I started to realize, like, oh.

00:14:55.820 --> 00:14:56.860
God damn it, Joe.

00:14:57.400 --> 00:14:59.000
Hey, I think I beat the game.

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:00.160
I think I broke the game.

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:02.320
What a pure commentary from Joe, though.

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:05.260
Like, fans of Metroid and fans of the show,

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:07.140
because most of the fans of the show have played Metroid,

00:15:07.140 --> 00:15:11.400
will know that this is Joe's honest-to-God first time playing this game.

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:12.600
Never before.

00:15:13.060 --> 00:15:14.660
Because he's said things like rockets.

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:16.240
What are they called?

00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:17.900
Missiles. What is that?

00:15:17.900 --> 00:15:19.140
I know. There's no difference,

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:23.600
but they've always been called missiles in the 14 Metroid games that exist.

00:15:23.780 --> 00:15:26.080
You know? It's just like a staple of the series.

00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:29.640
I like it. No, I'm saying this is proof that you were-

00:15:29.640 --> 00:15:33.720
I feel like there's a status I haven't reached of a Metroid fan that I gotta get into.

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:35.460
You didn't really grow up with Nintendo, right?

00:15:35.840 --> 00:15:37.440
I had an NES growing up.

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:39.960
And then at that point, moved on to PlayStation.

00:15:40.420 --> 00:15:44.940
Gotcha. But yeah, I will be calling a lot of things the wrong things throughout the episode.

00:15:45.180 --> 00:15:48.060
And Sam, what is your experience with Metroid?

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:50.660
Metroid. I played Metroid Prime.

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:52.400
Okay. And that's it.

00:15:52.820 --> 00:15:56.180
Wow, okay. So you come from a totally different background of Metroid,

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:58.080
where you're only used to the 3D version.

00:15:58.340 --> 00:16:02.960
Yeah. How did this very first entry-level 2D thing handle for you?

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:05.860
I had seen people play Metroid before.

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:06.900
Sure, it's hard to escape.

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:09.820
Super Metroid. And so I know what it is.

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:13.520
But I thought that it felt cool.

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:16.080
It feels cool before it gets frustrating.

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:21.240
But I think that one thing that they really nailed this time,

00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:23.700
which they did with Super Mario Bros., is the jump.

00:16:23.980 --> 00:16:26.200
I think the jump, again, is really satisfying.

00:16:26.820 --> 00:16:29.080
And you can tap it lightly for a small jump.

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:33.120
And your character is really floaty, which gives you that outer space feel.

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:35.600
Yeah, there is kind of like a zero gravity.

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:38.060
If you think about how many flips she's doing in the air,

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:40.180
it's like there must be some kind of zero.

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:41.340
You get like a moon gravity.

00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:42.760
That's got a hurt after a while.

00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:45.640
You're doing like eight front flips every single time you jump.

00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:49.540
Yeah. So I think that the jump really helps make the game.

00:16:49.760 --> 00:16:51.920
And you think Samus, you think about the weapons.

00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:53.960
But I think that the jump was really,

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:57.160
it couldn't be a good game without a satisfying jump.

00:16:57.320 --> 00:17:03.120
For you, is this game more about action, exploration, or platforming?

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:06.140
For me, it's about not getting hit.

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:09.960
Okay. Because you can't really do any of it without that.

00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:13.400
But I guess that's more because I'm new and bad.

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:16.780
But I would say more exploration.

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:19.260
Because, you know, you just get lost.

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:23.780
But a lot of it's just you've managed to barely get to the end of a corridor.

00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:26.800
And then you can't progress anymore.

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:27.940
And so you got to go back.

00:17:28.760 --> 00:17:33.480
Sean and Joe, any additional thoughts on action, exploration, or platforming?

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:35.340
Obviously, it is all three of those.

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:38.200
But which one were you kind of feeling as you were playing through the game?

00:17:38.400 --> 00:17:41.440
Well, I'm going to go more on exploration as well.

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:50.900
Simply because, like, this is a very different feel for me in terms of any game I've played with Samus in it.

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:58.900
Because up until this, I hadn't really given more than five minutes to a Metroid game other than, like, Smash.

00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:01.100
Like, I played with her as Smash.

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:06.960
And that was all I really knew of Samus until I popped this in.

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:10.480
And it's just a, it's sort of like a mood whiplash.

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:20.020
You're going from this really quick, like, Twitch environment to, oh, now I'm, like, walking down a dark hallway and falling down this crevasse.

00:18:20.020 --> 00:18:23.000
And I have to, like, I have to take my time and, like, try to explore.

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:25.000
Yeah. So I'd say exploration.

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:29.460
I think I kind of live somewhere between exploration and platforming.

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:34.360
Because my initial thought about the game was that the movement was so good.

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:36.180
And, like Sam was saying, the jumping was so good.

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:38.620
I feel like the platforming really kind of, like, shone.

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:40.340
Shined? Shined.

00:18:40.440 --> 00:18:41.540
I think shined is the right word.

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:44.820
But, you see, I won't even get real words right.

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:45.980
Not even just Metroid words.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:53.360
But then. And I also kind of, like, my first thing that I was thinking about this game in general was, it might be a little silly to compare,

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:56.820
but it was giving me a little bit of a Gradius feel as far as, like, the level of polish.

00:18:57.040 --> 00:19:02.520
I want to hear more. Like, just as far as, like, Gradius was our first, what is it, a shmup?

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:09.040
Yeah. That kind of had that level of polish and that level of, like, the look of it and also just, like, the motion of it.

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:14.360
And I feel like this is not the first, but the first in a while platformer that we've had with that same level.

00:19:14.520 --> 00:19:17.120
It feels like that level of care and that level of thought was put into it.

00:19:17.360 --> 00:19:19.500
Right. The power-ups and the movement and everything.

00:19:19.780 --> 00:19:23.720
Yeah, I think, I mean, we should talk about the power-ups and just the progression in general, guys.

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:33.380
Because if there's one thing this game does, you know, like, probably really well is the ability to make you feel like you're actually getting stronger throughout.

00:19:33.580 --> 00:19:40.660
We had a big complaint about this with Rygar, if you guys remember, where it was like, okay, I'm getting these power-ups, but they're only useful in, like, one situation.

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:52.020
Right. After, like, getting strong for a while and, like, you know, having more energy tanks and more missiles and I think, like, the wave beam is one that, like, really helps you feel powerful.

00:19:52.280 --> 00:20:00.140
Once you, like, go back and start with a new file, you realize, like, wow, this is a tough place for one person to be, you know?

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:01.940
Like, you only have, like, 35 energy.

00:20:02.420 --> 00:20:03.640
Everything's coming out to get you.

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:07.420
It's like, how did I survive at first without all this gear?

00:20:07.420 --> 00:20:10.680
It nails the feel of having a super suit.

00:20:10.920 --> 00:20:20.340
Like, it nails the feel of having, like, a robotic super suit and still, like, feels challenging and still feels like you're, you still feel like you're the underdog in the situation.

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:32.840
Well, that's what I like about it, too, is that because the progression is kind of locked behind, like, hey, you got to make sure you get this thing, but still allowing you to explore, like, other worlds or other areas within that world.

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:46.280
You know, you can go to Norfair or Brinstar, well, Brinstar's where you start, but you can go to Norfair or Torian, like, those places are available to you, but a lot of things that happen there are just, like, really hard.

00:20:46.400 --> 00:20:48.080
Like, enemies take forever to die.

00:20:48.360 --> 00:20:51.460
If you, you know, if you just go in down to Norfair, that's the purple one.

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:54.640
If you just go in there, you could get killed easily.

00:20:54.640 --> 00:21:00.980
Yeah, like, I got, well, not one-shotted, but it was quick when I ducked in there, like, oh, well, I guess I'm not going there anytime soon.

00:21:01.020 --> 00:21:05.220
Right, and then fast forward and you get all your power-ups and you're like, hey, I'm ready to deal with this place.

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:16.640
Yeah, and I think another thing that makes you feel more powerful in this game is all of the, like, you don't just fall into pits and die in this one.

00:21:16.940 --> 00:21:17.780
Like, if you fall into...

00:21:17.780 --> 00:21:18.840
There's actually no pits, right?

00:21:19.060 --> 00:21:20.100
Yeah, yeah. That's what I mean.

00:21:20.100 --> 00:21:29.800
Like, if you fall into lava, you would think, like, oh, you're, like, the entire game is going to, like, pause and then your character is going to do a silly face and fall off the screen.

00:21:30.480 --> 00:21:33.680
No, you just sort of, like, take damage for a while, but then you can get back up.

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:35.380
Like, that sells the power suit.

00:21:35.700 --> 00:21:36.600
It's not even that much damage also.

00:21:36.840 --> 00:21:42.660
No, it doesn't. It's, like, one damage per, not a set, like, half second that you're in there, which is less than enemies do.

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:49.840
And I think that's one of the parts of this game that is a lot more forgiving than a lot of, like, the Nintendo games we've played so far.

00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:53.180
Yeah, I think it does. While there are a lot of parts of this game that are not so forgiving.

00:21:53.400 --> 00:22:07.460
I have to interrupt for a second, because you couldn't be more spot on with what you're talking about, because Sakamoto and Kiyotake gave an interview for Nintendo when they were releasing the NES Classic for Metroid with the 30th anniversary and everything.

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:11.860
And they said that they were trying to make what Super Mario Bros.

00:22:12.180 --> 00:22:16.020
didn't have. So, the Nintendo employee asked...

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:17.980
Bottoms of pits. Yeah, like, what Super Mario Bros.

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:19.080
didn't have, like, what?

00:22:19.080 --> 00:22:24.160
And Kiyotake answers, as a simple example, you know how Mario slides a little bit before stopping?

00:22:24.980 --> 00:22:26.620
So, we tried to make a dead halt.

00:22:27.600 --> 00:22:32.660
Right? And it's like, and I thought, like, wow, that is a very obscure answer, but not unlike Nintendo employees.

00:22:32.680 --> 00:22:33.900
It doesn't explain why they're doing that.

00:22:33.900 --> 00:22:35.400
It's a much more vertical game.

00:22:35.440 --> 00:22:37.980
So, that makes sense. Yeah, and then goes into...

00:22:37.980 --> 00:22:40.380
But the real point, you know, trying to make what Super Mario Bros.

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:43.580
didn't have was they were like, well, Mario's trying to avoid the enemies.

00:22:43.580 --> 00:22:45.680
Why do I have to avoid the enemies?

00:22:46.140 --> 00:22:53.980
You know, like, the idea, you know, and it could have been a one hit or two hit kind of thing where, like, Samus, you know, the first time you get hit, you lose your armor.

00:22:54.220 --> 00:22:55.780
And then the second time you get hit, you die.

00:22:55.880 --> 00:22:57.780
You know, it's like, that could have been a thing.

00:22:57.780 --> 00:23:07.300
But they chose to make it a health-based system because they didn't want to have, you know, you locked around the idea of, like, everything is dangerous and I need to get out of here.

00:23:07.460 --> 00:23:15.180
They wanted you to give some power, some feel to, like, I'm going to explore the nooks and crannies and not be so afraid of taking a hit because I got to get close to my enemy.

00:23:15.380 --> 00:23:27.220
Is this the first game where we've had, like, an actual large value as our health instead of, like, not just, like, a one, two, three, like, one hit, two hit, three hit, but, like, actually, like, a large value that's good at training?

00:23:27.220 --> 00:23:31.100
Yeah. Between, like, Castlevania, which had at least, like, 20 bars.

00:23:31.360 --> 00:23:35.500
That's true. But it's still a health, I mean, just, like, it's a health bar and now we just have, like, a number.

00:23:35.640 --> 00:23:40.100
Well, yeah, we recently played the other shmup.

00:23:40.680 --> 00:23:41.700
There's another shmup?

00:23:41.820 --> 00:23:43.080
Oh, yeah, Section Z?

00:23:43.120 --> 00:23:49.460
Section Z had, like, energy in the, I mean, you could, when you got hit by things, you still died, but you could take a bunch of bullets.

00:23:49.480 --> 00:23:51.980
That's right. That's the first example of a numbered thing.

00:23:52.060 --> 00:23:53.140
I'm surprised you actually remembered that.

00:23:53.200 --> 00:23:54.580
That was good for you to remember.

00:23:54.580 --> 00:24:01.220
But I think one thing that Joe mentioned, one thing that Joe mentioned is the large number.

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:08.920
Like, that's something that we haven't seen before because you could be in any of those games and, like, yeah, like, some of them are, like, 16 hits and that feels great.

00:24:09.120 --> 00:24:17.160
But towards the end of this game, you could have 500 energy or more even, 500 energy, and that takes a while to deplete.

00:24:17.160 --> 00:24:22.900
The problem is that once it depletes that first time, good luck ever getting it back.

00:24:22.900 --> 00:24:25.720
I hope you have five hours to grind and get your energy back up.

00:24:25.980 --> 00:24:27.920
Energy is a huge problem in this game.

00:24:27.920 --> 00:24:29.880
It's my first official problem with Metroid.

00:24:30.160 --> 00:24:39.180
You know, I will have some more, but since we've been so nice to the game, I'm going to get a little critical for a second and talk about how I don't really like the energy system.

00:24:39.180 --> 00:24:44.860
If only because enemies take more damage than they give.

00:24:45.440 --> 00:24:51.860
A lot of enemies that you get hit by will then, if you, like, receive energy from them, you won't get back enough energy.

00:24:51.860 --> 00:24:54.760
So they deal more damage to you than they give out.

00:24:54.760 --> 00:25:00.020
Right, exactly. And on top of that, not everyone is guaranteed to give you energy, which is fine.

00:25:00.020 --> 00:25:02.200
Not, you know, it shouldn't just be a free health game.

00:25:02.760 --> 00:25:04.260
You know, this isn't free health care.

00:25:05.040 --> 00:25:10.680
But, whoa. But hot take, you know, the Galactic Federation should give us all health care.

00:25:11.520 --> 00:25:26.980
But the, what I was talking about is the idea that once you have 500 energy, like five energy tanks and 500 health, and then you go down to like, or even just restart your game, put it in, put in the password and spawn back at the beginning.

00:25:27.220 --> 00:25:29.580
You spawn with only 35 health.

00:25:29.580 --> 00:25:30.560
With the, oh, yeah.

00:25:30.680 --> 00:25:32.200
With the energy bars don't stay filled.

00:25:32.380 --> 00:25:34.500
You will never fill those things back up.

00:25:34.600 --> 00:25:38.940
I don't care. Like, you need so much time to fill up 500 energy in this game.

00:25:38.980 --> 00:25:42.820
And I know about those bugs that come out of the very similar looking warp pipes.

00:25:43.280 --> 00:25:44.900
Yeah. They do kind of look like warp pipes.

00:25:45.100 --> 00:25:50.000
I think they're air vents. I know about those bugs that come out of that and you shoot them and they're most likely going to give you health.

00:25:50.180 --> 00:25:51.920
Like, one in three times they're going to give you health.

00:25:52.160 --> 00:25:53.520
But, Joe, how much is it?

00:25:53.600 --> 00:25:57.620
Like, four? Yeah, I found that very helpful at the beginning when I had 99 health.

00:25:57.800 --> 00:25:58.800
And I could sit there four.

00:25:58.800 --> 00:26:00.660
It still took me like six minutes.

00:26:01.000 --> 00:26:03.300
So, yeah. So, amplify that by times five.

00:26:03.580 --> 00:26:05.100
I do not have the time for that.

00:26:05.160 --> 00:26:10.200
No. You don't have 30 minutes to get back to 500 health because that's how I'm going to take down Ridley.

00:26:10.380 --> 00:26:15.060
And also in those little areas, there's usually more stuff going on than just those little air vents.

00:26:15.060 --> 00:26:20.260
Right. There's usually stuff flying at you that's taking away health as you're trying to gain it.

00:26:20.360 --> 00:26:26.620
That was the thing that happened to me a couple times where I said, oh, okay, I'll just post up in front of this little air vent thing.

00:26:26.700 --> 00:26:27.780
Shoot these bugs and get health.

00:26:28.340 --> 00:26:30.220
And meanwhile, I'm getting attacked by a bunch of other stuff.

00:26:30.220 --> 00:26:35.040
But, and also, when you want to go get the health, you have to stand on the air vent, but they don't stop coming.

00:26:35.580 --> 00:26:38.080
You know? You have to jump and grab it.

00:26:38.520 --> 00:26:41.940
So, I was getting hit as I was trying to get the health from the guys.

00:26:42.400 --> 00:26:46.320
You've got to plan it. Yeah, I was leading them to wait until they got close to me and then hit them.

00:26:46.420 --> 00:26:47.500
So, then the health dropped in front of me.

00:26:47.500 --> 00:26:51.000
But that's just too long. So, Sam, you talked about the verticality of this game.

00:26:51.160 --> 00:26:54.720
Yeah. There's a lot of vertical scrolling instead of horizontal.

00:26:54.960 --> 00:26:56.640
But, I mean, both of them are there.

00:27:02.980 --> 00:27:05.440
I just want to talk about map layout in general.

00:27:05.740 --> 00:27:10.380
You know, we don't have to get specific about, like, the map layout of Brinestar versus the map layout of Norfair.

00:27:10.500 --> 00:27:12.760
But, like, what did you guys think of the map?

00:27:12.760 --> 00:27:22.960
Well, one, the fact that there is no, like, visual map is something that, as a player in this day and age, I find very frustrating.

00:27:23.260 --> 00:27:25.460
I'm not really a mental map kind of guy.

00:27:25.460 --> 00:27:26.580
You didn't try graph paper?

00:27:26.860 --> 00:27:33.920
No. That is a valid thing to do, but I'm not expecting anybody to bust out the graph paper and map it out.

00:27:33.980 --> 00:27:38.620
And I guess, like, I could have just pulled up, like, a PDF of the map on my computer.

00:27:38.840 --> 00:27:40.220
But is that fun? It's not.

00:27:40.920 --> 00:27:45.380
And I know that, like, I know that, oh, but what, okay, so you've got it in the game.

00:27:45.560 --> 00:27:46.940
Is that fun either?

00:27:47.100 --> 00:27:50.740
But, like, at least show me what I've explored yet.

00:27:50.740 --> 00:27:55.820
I know that they did fix that or at least add that in the remake for the GBA.

00:27:55.940 --> 00:28:00.100
Yeah, and even Super Metroid, which will be the next console game for Metroid.

00:28:00.380 --> 00:28:08.360
Even Super Metroid does have it where, exactly as you're describing, where you don't get to see the rest of the map, only the areas that you've actually touched.

00:28:08.620 --> 00:28:16.820
Yeah. And not saying that this is necessarily a good thing, but I think that what, to me, it felt like what they're trying to go for is, like, yeah, you're lost in this place.

00:28:16.960 --> 00:28:20.200
Like, I feel like it was going for the feel of, like, you're lost.

00:28:20.380 --> 00:28:25.820
And I did start to feel like after a while I was starting to get, like, oh, okay, I know where I am.

00:28:26.060 --> 00:28:29.560
Because basically, like, that was kind of a cool feeling to, like, be familiar with an area.

00:28:29.560 --> 00:28:34.180
